# Build-context exclusions for both Dockerfile.api and Dockerfile.dashboard.
#
# The model store (mlruns.db, mlartifacts/) and the processed feature
# dataset (data/processed/) are intentionally NOT baked into either image
# -- they are git-ignored, developer/environment-generated artifacts (see
# .gitignore), so they are supplied to the containers as read-only bind
# mounts in docker-compose.yml instead. This keeps the images small,
# generic, and rebuildable without needing to re-copy ~25MB of local
# state, and means a missing artifact fails clearly at container startup
# (via the existing ModelService/FastAPI health check) rather than being
# silently baked into a stale image layer.

.git/
.github/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.env
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
mlruns/
mlartifacts/
*.db
*.pkl
*.joblib
catboost_info/

# Supplied via docker-compose.yml volume mounts at runtime, not copied
# into the image -- see note above.
data/raw/
data/processed/
data/external/

# Large generated inference output (~50MB+), never needed by the API or
# dashboard containers (matches .gitignore).
reports/customer_recommendations.csv

# Not needed inside either running container.
notebooks/
tests/
